.TH "CITADEL" "1" "Sep 2026" "AceTeam" "Citadel CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
citadel-tmux - Manage the Citadel-managed tmux binary for persistent terminal sessions


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcitadel tmux [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Persistent, reconnect-resilient terminal sessions ("chat to a node") are
backed by tmux. Citadel never assumes tmux is installed: it looks for tmux via
CITADEL_TMUX_BIN, then PATH, then a Citadel-managed binary. These commands manage
that Citadel-managed binary.

.PP
If no usable tmux is found, the terminal server falls back to a bare,
non-persistent shell.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for tmux


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug output

.PP
\fB--no-auto-update\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic update checks and installs for this run (or set CITADEL_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colorized output

.PP
\fB--node-dir\fP=""
	Override the node config directory (citadel.yaml + services/), bypassing $HOME/ConfigDir resolution. Also settable via CITADEL_NODE_DIR. Scope: manifest/services resolution only -- does NOT redirect network state, the module lockfile, or nodevault.

.PP
\fB--runtime\fP=""
	Container runtime for module containers: docker or podman (default: auto-detect)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcitadel(1)\fP, \fBcitadel-tmux-install(1)\fP, \fBcitadel-tmux-status(1)\fP
